  "body": "## What changed\n\nA **Cut** pipeline that runs the release gate tier on the self-hosted Linux runner and then **triggers the existing `release.yml`** for the tag. It does not replace `release.yml`: that file is unchanged (its jobs, runners and publishing as they are). It already has a `workflow_dispatch` trigger, so not even a trigger had to be added.\n\n- **`.github/workflows/cut.yml`** (new). Trigger: `workflow_dispatch` only. Inputs: `version` (X.Y.0), `stage` (`gate` | `tag`) and `dry_run`. Every job is `runs-on: [self-hosted, linux]`. `concurrency: cut` allows one cut at a time and never cancels a running one.\n  - `stage: gate` runs before the release PR merges. It checks out `release/vX.Y.0` with `persist-credentials: false`, so no token is on disk while tests run. It refuses a branch whose `Cargo.toml` or `RELEASE_NOTES.md` doesn't name the version, or whose tag already exists. Then it runs `cargo xtask gate release --no-snapshots`, inside `xvfb-run -a` when there is no display. It always uploads `gate-logs/` and `gate-output.txt` as an artifact and writes the gate summary to the job summary. When green and not a dry run, it uploads the tested commit as `cut-tip-vX.Y.0`. It tags nothing.\n  - `stage: tag` runs after the release PR merged. It finds the newest green gate run for the version and takes its tip. It refuses unless main's head `m` is the release PR's merge of that tip (`m^2 == tip`), `git diff $tip $m` is empty (AGENTS.md step 4's rule, kept), the tag is free on origin and `Cargo.toml` names the version. It then runs `git tag -a vX.Y.0 $m`, pushes the tag, and runs **`gh workflow run release.yml --ref vX.Y.0`** with `GITHUB_TOKEN`. A tag pushed with `GITHUB_TOKEN` starts no workflow by itself; a `workflow_dispatch` from it does. On a tag ref, release.yml's `publish` and `pages` see `refs/tags/...` exactly as they do on a pushed tag. Only this job has `contents: write` and `actions: write`.\n  - `dry_run`: the gate stage prints its plan (`--dry-run`); the tag stage runs every check and stops before the tag and the dispatch.\n- **xtask**: `cargo xtask gate release --no-snapshots` is the release plan without the two pixel-snapshot lanes (`--lib --ignored snapshot` and `--test gpu_render --ignored snapshot`). The flag is refused on any other tier. Pinned by `release_without_snapshots_drops_only_the_pixel_lanes`.\n- **AGENTS.md**:\n  - the release tier entry in the gate tiers list\n  - \"GitHub Actions minutes are budgeted\": self-hosted jobs bill nothing, triggers stay `workflow_dispatch`, no fork-triggerable trigger on a self-hosted workflow, and the billed minutes of one cut, with a placeholder to fill in from the first real cut\n  - new \"The cut runner\" section: requirements, registration and safety, written generically with no host-specific names\n  - cut steps 2-4 and \"Every cut tag is published\"\n  - the local cut stays as the fallback when the runner is down\n- **`.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`** 54 -> 55 (process files: AGENTS.md, xtask). The final number is settled at merge.\n- **`docs/decisions/1413-cut-pipeline.md`**: the decisions below.\n\n## Open questions settled (details in the decision file)\n\n- **Where the tag is made.** The gate runs on the release branch tip before the release PR merges, so a red gate leaves no untagged release on main. A second dispatch (`stage: tag`) after the merge checks `m^2 == tip` and that `git diff $tip $m` is empty, then tags. The empty-diff rule is kept and is now machine-checked.\n- **Windows-only pinned readings** (issue 1402's per-OS move counts). The Linux gate checks only the Linux arm. A local Windows check stays **optional** at a cut, named in step 2. If nobody runs it, the Windows arm drifts until the next Windows run, and the release PR says it was skipped.\n- **UI snapshot lane on Linux.** Skipped on Linux (`--no-snapshots`) and kept as a local Windows step at the cut. The goldens are Windows renders, and a GPU-less Mesa render would differ in pixels every cut, or need a second set of goldens kept in step. Their structural twins still run in the ui suites on Linux.\n- **Version bump, zip, installer.**\n  - The bump stays local on the release branch: `cargo xtask release --version X.Y.0 --no-tag --skip-gate`.\n  - `release.yml` already builds the published zip, installer and packages from the tag, and nothing about that changes.\n  - The local zip and installer are now a hand-test build only.\n  - The installer stays Windows-only, in release.yml's Windows job.\n\n## Runner (already registered)\n\nAGENTS.md lists the requirements generically: Linux x64, labels `self-hosted`/`Linux`/`X64`, disk of at least 100 GB, the toolchain on the service PATH, `git` and `gh`, the build packages from release.yml's linux job, `xvfb` plus Mesa software drivers, and sccache configured in `.env` with no `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`. It also gives the `config.sh` registration and the service setup. **Runner prerequisite to check:** `gh`, `xvfb` and the Mesa and dev packages must be installed on the box. The workflow can't install them, because the runner has no sudo.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `actionlint` 1.7.12 (release binary in a scratch dir, sha256 checked against the release's checksums file, not added to the repo): clean on `cut.yml` and every other workflow. shellcheck was not installed, so the `run:` scripts were not shellchecked.\n- YAML parse (Ruby Psych): trigger `workflow_dispatch` only; inputs `version`, `stage`, `dry_run`; jobs `gate` and `tag`, both `[self-hosted, linux]`.\n- `cargo xtask gate release --no-snapshots --dry-run`: 12 steps, namely every debug suite (kernel included), ui, clippy, and the motion and app heavy lanes, with no snapshot lane.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: xtask unit tests 90 passed, 1 failed. The one failure is `gate_maps_tests::no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app`, which **already fails on a clean upstream/main 3f6ecb4a** (ten test headers name moved modules as `app::`), so this PR did not cause it. Filed as #1417. With that test skipped, all 90 pass, including `release_without_snapshots_drops_only_the_pixel_lanes`, `batch_skips_slow_binaries_and_release_runs_everything` and `cli_parses_the_gate_forms`.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No product Rust code changed.\n\n## Not exercised: maintainer's post-merge check\n\nA workflow can only be dispatched once it is on the default branch, so **no real run happened**: not the runner, not xvfb or the UI suites under it, not the artifact hand-off between stages, not the tag push or the release.yml dispatch. After merge, run in this order:\n\n1. `gh workflow run cut.yml -R NeoTech/Camcraft -f version=<test X.Y.0> -f stage=gate -f dry_run=true` checks the runner picks the job up and prints the plan (it needs a `release/v<test>` branch whose Cargo.toml and RELEASE_NOTES.md name the version).\n2. The same command without `dry_run` runs the real gate. Expect about 75 min or less. It should prove the UI suites pass under xvfb. A deliberately red commit on the scratch branch should also make no tag (step 3 refuses, since there is no green gate run).\n3. After the scratch release PR merges (or on a throwaway fork): `gh workflow run cut.yml -R NeoTech/Camcraft -f version=<test> -f stage=tag -f dry_run=true`, then the same command without `dry_run`. Check that the tag lands on the merge commit and that release.yml starts on the tag and attaches its artifacts to the GitHub release. Then fill in AGENTS.md's \"measured cut\" placeholder from that run's Usage. Branch protection and tag rulesets must allow `github-actions[bot]` to push tags.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n`.github` change: expected to get `needs-maintainer` at review.\n\nFixes #1413\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
